     <rdf:li>Tokyo Midtown Hibiya</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li>commercial complex</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li>Hibiya</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li>shopping mall</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li>building</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li>Mitsui Fudosan</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li>Toho Cinemas</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li>IMAX screen</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Bag>
   </dc:subject>
   <dc:description>
    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Toho Cinemas theater at Tokyo Midtown Hibiya shopping mall during a media event on March 22, 2018, Tokyo Japan. Located near Hibiya Park and the luxury district of Ginza, the new 35-story building by Mitsui Fudosan Realty houses office and shopping center. Tokyo Midtown Hibiya will be open to the public on March 29. (Photo by Rodrigo Reyes Marin/AFLO)</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:description>
